Canonical scene-render schema, vendored unchanged from sr-core
(https://github.com/pedroanisio/sr-core), release 1.3.0: the annotated tag schema-1.3.0, commit
56a9ad3d7761f037b7a752215563cbfb5a163ce5 (branch release/schema-1.3). Schema 1.2.0 is the annotated tag schema-1.2.0,
commit d02d6cd4b581f15baa15aef1c3fcdd501d4f7040 (branch release/schema-1.2). The schema files of the tag are the ones
below (checked: the sha256 of schema/scene-render.xsd and .sch at the tag equals the values here).

  scene-render-1.1.xsd  <- schema/scene-render.xsd  sha256 0975936b28417611f6a00197a87bd398d6e2336b197aaf5e634d88f335013075
  scene-render-1.1.sch  <- schema/scene-render.sch  sha256 e84979657842c2d84550d0900c089fd607d965a06b8441318978f1bd88de7d38

The files change only through an accepted SREP in sr-core (srep/, process in srep/srep-0000.md); a new release is
vendored here by replacing both files and updating this record. (The local file names keep "1.1" for the tools that
read them; the schema documents declare version 1.0 to 1.3.)

SREPs in this release: 9 to 11, 13, 15 to 21, 23, 24 and 26 to 39, 41 to 56 (schema 1.2.0); 40 (schema 1.3.0).

Accepted but not implemented by this engine yet (a use is reported as warning E22, which --strict counts; the table
is crates/sr-eval/src/pending.rs, and each implementing branch deletes its own row): 16 (connectors), 17 (PDF pages
and regions), 18 (render reports), 19 (legibility checks), 21 (pinned-font policy), 26 (repeat points). Their rules
(C60 to C64, C66 to C80, R48 to R52, V9 to V11) are in the schema and not mirrored in rules.rs; the corpus coverage
test lists them (PENDING_RULES in crates/sr-model/tests/corpus.rs).

Rule ids the engine emits keep their numbers. The grid lineWidth rule is R47 (SREP 30; R45 and R46 belong to SREP 17).

The engine's differences from the canonical text are recorded in PALS-Notes/projects/sr-core-schema-1.3/work/DIFF.md.

Added here, not in sr-core 1.3.0 (SREP 0 of this repository, the cinematic proposal, srep-0000-cinematic-impact.md):
the elements blackHole and accretionDisk (blackHoleType, accretionDiskType; rules BH1 to BH8), camera/@geodesics,
fracture/@source, fracture/@minImpulse and fracture/@energyFraction (rules FRX5 to FRX7), ocean/@density, and crater/@mantle, crater/@bulking and crater/@repose (rules CRT10 to CRT12); the
rest of the cinematic families (OCN, P3D, CRT, PYC, PYRO, VOL, FRX, MSQ, GEO) is in sr-core 1.3.0 as released. A
release of sr-core that takes these in replaces them; until then a vendoring keeps them (the merge of
2026-10-06 was done by component: every top-level type, group and pattern that sr-core changed since the previous
vendoring is theirs, every one that only this repository changed is ours, and nothing was changed by both).
